  message: "WI-jukav slice 2 verification complete; no code PR required.\n\nVerification per the swift-jingling-pearl PR-1 plan:\n- `is_excluded_kind()` at selection/filters.py:102-137 is already on the slice-1 dual-predicate shape (shipped in commit d518994f3a).\n- CONTAINABLE_KINDS / CONTAINER_KINDS at linkers/containment.py:76,88-91 carry audit comments documenting the ADR-0027 Phase-2 verdict 'no dual-shape predicate needed' (post-fold canonicals already in both sets).\n- Sweep of other hardcoded kind sets:\n  * entrypoints.py:992 `_CALLABLE_KINDS = {function, method, constructor}` — canonical-only, no Wave 8 impact.\n  * ranking.py:888,953 `_CALLABLE_KINDS = {function, method}` — canonical-only, no Wave 8 impact.\n  * slice.py:533 `_CONTAINER_KINDS` — canonical-only with intentional narrowness audit comment.\n  * sketch.py:5496-5525 `KEY_SYMBOL_KINDS` — curated cross-language declaration set (not a registry-axis query); contains `structure` (Cluster C peer) and `stage` (Cluster G), which Wave 8 PR 3 will drop via the EXCLUDED_KINDS-style sweep.\n\nEXCLUDED_KINDS at selection/filters.py:78-99 keeps the legacy literals through the Phase 4a deprecation window per its top-of-set comment; PR 3 (Symbol.kind Phase 4b) drops them alongside the SYMBOL_KINDS removals.\n\nStatus update lag — closing in support of WI-runod Wave 2 cleanup."  # 0b88
